1
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:42,120
Number 0011, please proceed to Window 3.

2
00:01:44,359 --> 00:01:45,000
She turned herself in.

3
00:01:45,519 --> 00:01:46,239
When did that happen?

4
00:01:48,239 --> 00:01:49,319
Last night, after work.

5
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:51,959
She confessed to everything.

6
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:53,560
You bet.

7
00:01:54,319 --> 00:01:56,840
Time, location, motive.

8
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:58,799
The old lady didn't hide a thing.

9
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:02,319
Then how does this count?

10
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:05,599
What? How does what count?

11
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:09,000
I mean, does this count as me solving the case?

12
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:11,840
Well, what do you think?

13
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,000
She turned herself in.

14
00:02:14,479 --> 00:02:15,639
How could it count as you solving it?

15
00:02:17,039 --> 00:02:18,719
At most, you just found some clues.

16
00:02:22,439 --> 00:02:24,120
Finding clues should count for something, right?

17
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:27,039
Yunsheng, you're obsessed with getting credit.

18
00:02:28,759 --> 00:02:29,840
This case is a bit special.

19
00:02:31,319 --> 00:02:32,159
Commissar Tan, you're here.

20
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,439
Have you had breakfast?

21
00:02:33,439 --> 00:02:34,520
I have. Thank you, Commissar Tan.

22
00:02:34,919 --> 00:02:35,560
You're welcome.

23
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,439
Commissar Tan, you're here.

24
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:43,639
Want some breakfast?

25
00:02:43,639 --> 00:02:44,719
I've had some. Thank you.

26
00:02:45,639 --> 00:02:46,280
Morning, Commissar Tan.

27
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:47,599
Morning, morning.

28
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,319
Morning, Commissar Tan.

29
00:02:48,879 --> 00:02:50,759
I bought some spiced boiled eggs.

30
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,919
Here, hand them out to everyone.

31
00:02:53,479 --> 00:02:54,639
Thank you, Commissar Tan. Thanks, Commissar.

32
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,159
You're welcome, you're welcome.

33
00:02:56,479 --> 00:02:58,039
What... what happened to your legs?

34
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:58,759
Were you on a mission?

35
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:00,960
Don't ask.

36
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,879
My legs and butt don't feel like my own.

37
00:03:03,879 --> 00:03:05,680
The training was too intense.

38
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:07,319
I overdid it.

39
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:08,280
You need to take it easy.

40
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,319
You're a commissar, no need to push so hard.

41
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,400
It's not like I want to.

42
00:03:12,199 --> 00:03:13,400
The chief is in his dorm.

43
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,240
Spiced eggs, have some.

44
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:16,199
Thank you, thank you.

45
00:03:16,879 --> 00:03:17,400
Morning, Commissar Tan.

46
00:03:18,199 --> 00:03:18,919
Who can eat all of this?

47
00:03:18,919 --> 00:03:20,599
Here, this is for everyone.

48
00:03:21,719 --> 00:03:22,759
Spiced boiled eggs.

49
00:03:23,599 --> 00:03:25,000
Mini fried dough.

50
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,639
Jianbing.

51
00:03:28,199 --> 00:03:29,520
Millet porridge.

52
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:31,159
Sesame balls.

53
00:03:31,639 --> 00:03:32,319
No steamed buns.

54
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,159
There's something for everyone.

55
00:03:41,319 --> 00:03:42,439
I've already had breakfast.

56
00:03:44,159 --> 00:03:45,360
You're not having any?

57
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:49,280
Well, we can't let it go to waste.

58
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:04,479
My legs and butt don't feel like my own.

59
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:11,039
Tan Yan, about us...

60
00:04:11,039 --> 00:04:13,719
We... we're not talking about us today.

61
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:23,879
We're talking about work.

62
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:29,199
What work?

63
00:04:30,319 --> 00:04:30,879
About

64
00:04:31,759 --> 00:04:32,519
Wang Yunsheng.

65
00:04:35,639 --> 00:04:36,920
Haven't we already talked about this?

66
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,240
If he wants to leave, I won't stop him.

67
00:04:42,399 --> 00:04:44,920
I heard about Dai Mingming's case.

68
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:46,639
I wanted to talk to you about it.

69
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:48,720
Talk about what?

70
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:54,279
Dai Mingming and his mother.

71
00:04:54,879 --> 00:04:56,120
It was Wang Yunsheng

72
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:57,319
who saved them.

73
00:04:58,279 --> 00:04:59,120
The clues

74
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,040
were also from him.

75
00:05:04,879 --> 00:05:07,240
Why are you excluding him now?

76
00:05:10,319 --> 00:05:11,800
How much do you know about this case?

77
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,000
A fair amount.

78
00:05:16,279 --> 00:05:17,800
A terminally ill elderly mother

79
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,959
with an intellectually disabled son.

80
00:05:20,519 --> 00:05:22,079
Feared her son couldn't survive alone,

81
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:25,319
so she wanted to die with him.

82
00:05:26,560 --> 00:05:27,639
It sounds heartbreaking.

83
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:29,319
Of course,

84
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:32,519
Chief Ji must have more details.

85
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:36,120
Dai Mingming's mom turned herself in.

86
00:05:40,519 --> 00:05:41,399
This case

87
00:05:42,079 --> 00:05:43,079
was originally

88
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:44,879
one where no one pressed charges.

89
00:05:46,879 --> 00:05:48,720
Hard to tell if it was suicide or murder.

90
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,720
So I had Wang Yunsheng assist Li Zhi.

91
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,879
We couldn't jump to conclusions.

92
00:05:55,439 --> 00:05:57,800
But Wang Yunsheng acted on his own.

93
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,480
He brought Dai Mingming to the station.

94
00:06:00,639 --> 00:06:01,839
Though you're off the front lines now,

95
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,040
you're still a veteran cop.

96
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,480
In this kind of situation,

97
00:06:05,959 --> 00:06:06,600
what do you think would happen?

98
00:06:06,639 --> 00:06:08,040
We'd have to investigate it to the end.

99
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:11,920
So do you still think

100
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,519
that me excluding Wang Yunsheng

101
00:06:13,759 --> 00:06:14,480
is a problem?

102
00:06:19,839 --> 00:06:20,959
When it comes to experience in this area,

103
00:06:21,759 --> 00:06:23,480
Wang Yunsheng is severely lacking.

104
00:06:27,759 --> 00:06:29,839
But he is the one who saved them.

105
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,040
I think this kid

106
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:34,720
can endure hardship,

107
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:36,439
has drive,

108
00:06:37,639 --> 00:06:40,160
and has great enthusiasm for police work.

109
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,360
That's very valuable.

110
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,959
He just lacks experience.

111
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:48,079
Experience needs to be accumulated.

112
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,639
Which requires us leaders

113
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,360
to give him opportunities.

114
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,360
It's hard for an auxiliary to go regular.

115
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,000
He'll get all the credit he deserves.

116
00:07:01,639 --> 00:07:03,079
I'll give him the chances he deserves.

117
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,360
There's one more thing you don't know.

118
00:07:13,879 --> 00:07:15,120
He's actually quite like you in this.

119
00:07:17,439 --> 00:07:18,160
In what way?

120
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:20,160
Eager for quick success.

121
00:07:24,439 --> 00:07:26,000
The sesame balls lack filling today.

122
00:07:26,959 --> 00:07:28,839
That old guy must've made them, look.

123
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:30,759
Do you need anything else?

124
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,079
If not, I'm going to change clothes.

125
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:33,560
Okay, go ahead.

126
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:35,319
I'll clean this up for you.

127
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:35,920
No need.

128
00:07:36,680 --> 00:07:37,240
Just go.

129
00:07:48,319 --> 00:07:49,319
I'll close the door for you.

130
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:01,480
Commissar Tan

131
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:04,440
Tomorrow we rappel at the fire station.

132
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,120
Are you going?

133
00:09:06,519 --> 00:09:07,000
Yeah, I'm going.

134
00:09:08,279 --> 00:09:09,080
That's great!

135
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,919
Eight stories. Not too high, but very fun.

136
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:12,960
You should give it a try.

137
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:14,679
Lu Xiao,

138
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,919
stop trying to get people hurt.

139
00:09:18,519 --> 00:09:20,200
Shoo, shoo. Stay away, stay away.

140
00:09:21,279 --> 00:09:23,519
Commissar Tan, don't listen to him.

141
00:09:23,679 --> 00:09:25,639
Rappelling is not like running.

142
00:09:25,639 --> 00:09:27,799
Man, it's not easy to pick up.

143
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,519
You might end up flipping over.

144
00:09:29,879 --> 00:09:31,519
Boss, you underestimate Commissar Tan.

145
00:09:31,759 --> 00:09:32,919
He kept up with the ten-kilometer run.

146
00:09:32,919 --> 00:09:33,879
He'll learn it in a couple of tries.

147
00:09:33,919 --> 00:09:34,879
How is that the same thing?

148
00:09:38,679 --> 00:09:40,000
I wasn't planning on trying it.

149
00:09:41,639 --> 00:09:42,879
Mainly just to observe and learn.

150
00:09:44,399 --> 00:09:45,000
You guys do it.

151
00:09:46,919 --> 00:09:47,879
Done showering, Commissar.

152
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:48,879
Done showering.

153
00:09:49,759 --> 00:09:50,720
Good night, good night.

154
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:56,679
Why aren't you pushing yourself anymore?

155
00:09:58,720 --> 00:09:59,639
Just lying flat, you know.

156
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:57,720
What's his time?

157
00:11:05,519 --> 00:11:06,600
Next group, let's go.

158
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:08,879
Lu Xiao.

159
00:11:09,759 --> 00:11:10,519
Set a new standard.

160
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:11,600
Set an example for everyone.

161
00:11:12,039 --> 00:11:12,919
Just watch, boss.

162
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:35,440
What's the time?

163
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:38,840
Captain Liao, a new record?

164
00:11:39,639 --> 00:11:40,480
Still a bit short.

165
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:45,600
Lu Xiao!

166
00:11:46,039 --> 00:11:46,799
You broke the record!

167
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,000
Faster by 0.8 seconds.

168
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,279
Not bad.

169
00:11:55,639 --> 00:11:56,200
Lu Xiao!

170
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:57,679
Don't let it get to your head.

171
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,320
This is a new starting point.

172
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,639
This is the new standard for the team.

173
00:12:01,960 --> 00:12:02,399
Do you hear me?

174
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,159
Yes, sir!

175
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:03,639
At ease.

176
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,679
Alright, take a 15-minute break.

177
00:12:08,279 --> 00:12:09,279
While we're taking a break,

178
00:12:09,320 --> 00:12:10,919
let's have a quick meeting.

179
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:20,120
You guys really opened my eyes.

180
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:24,000
Lu Xiao,

181
00:12:24,879 --> 00:12:26,639
you're really fast.

182
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,080
You're light on your feet.

183
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:30,240
I even suspect you stomped that wall

184
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,799
and made it a few centimeters shorter.

185
00:12:35,639 --> 00:12:37,159
Liu Lang, what you just said,

186
00:12:37,559 --> 00:12:39,240
about reaching a new starting point,

187
00:12:39,559 --> 00:12:40,559
was well said.

188
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,240
It pushed our goal a big step forward.

189
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,000
Exactly.

190
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:46,440
Improving by 0.8 seconds isn't easy.

191
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:49,399
With a benchmark like you on the team,

192
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,080
how could this team

193
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,720
not be motivated to improve?

194
00:12:54,960 --> 00:12:55,840
Bai Jiani,

195
00:12:56,639 --> 00:12:59,279
the only female officer on our SWAT team.

196
00:12:59,639 --> 00:13:01,559
Your rappelling was incredibly swift.

197
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:03,080
Even swifter

198
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:03,960
than the moves

199
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,240
by our foreign counterparts

200
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:05,960
I've seen in documentaries.

201
00:13:07,159 --> 00:13:07,960
Outstanding.

202
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:08,679
Thank you, Commissar.

203
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,120
Our SWAT team's

204
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,240
current combat effectiveness

205
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:14,679
couldn't have been achieved

206
00:13:15,039 --> 00:13:16,039
without everyone's hard work.

207
00:13:17,639 --> 00:13:20,080
Improving team quality to excellence...

208
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:22,799
that is what makes us truly formidable.

209
00:13:23,679 --> 00:13:24,879
I mean every word I say.

210
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:28,559
I also hope everyone speaks their minds.

211
00:13:29,279 --> 00:13:31,679
No matter what problems,

212
00:13:31,679 --> 00:13:32,480
difficulties,

213
00:13:32,759 --> 00:13:33,919
or differing opinions you have,

214
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,360
bring them up boldly.

215
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,799
Lu Xiao, say a few words.

216
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:53,360
I think this training ground is great.

217
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:55,720
Training here helped me break the record.

218
00:13:56,639 --> 00:13:58,559
But our SWAT team doesn't have one.

219
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:00,080
Right.

220
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,840
We don't have one.

221
00:14:04,559 --> 00:14:07,240
But we have an intense training regimen.

222
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,759
Without intense training,

223
00:14:10,159 --> 00:14:11,360
could you have broken the record?

224
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,200
If it's just about the facility,

225
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,480
why didn't they break the record?

226
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,200
Judging from your performance,

227
00:14:19,679 --> 00:14:21,440
relying solely on physical training

228
00:14:23,399 --> 00:14:24,919
is no longer enough to meet

229
00:14:24,919 --> 00:14:26,720
the demands of future challenges.

230
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,840
The team's overall quality,

231
00:14:30,279 --> 00:14:33,080
especially ideological discipline,

232
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:34,320
in my opinion,

233
00:14:35,159 --> 00:14:37,120
is more important than physical fitness.

234
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:40,639
Commissar,

235
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,480
how do we discipline our minds?

236
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,279
Well, here's what I think.

237
00:14:49,279 --> 00:14:51,120
While we strengthen our bodies,

238
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,399
we should elevate our minds.

239
00:14:53,879 --> 00:14:56,559
We'll resume the weekly meetings

240
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:58,600
and ideological classes.

241
00:14:59,519 --> 00:15:01,519
Submit a reflection report every 3 days.

242
00:15:02,759 --> 00:15:05,840
Share takeaways from life and training.

243
00:15:06,480 --> 00:15:10,000
You can even write about your frustrations.

244
00:15:11,279 --> 00:15:12,759
I'll review and comment on every one.

245
00:15:13,200 --> 00:15:14,240
And grade them, too.

246
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:17,480
One every three days, ten a month.

247
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:20,120
Harder than at the Police University.

248
00:15:20,559 --> 00:15:21,559
It's not demanding.

249
00:15:22,679 --> 00:15:24,559
Come on, next item, climbing!

250
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:25,200
Fall in!

251
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:38,200
Boss.

252
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:41,240
What's Old Tan playing at?

253
00:15:41,799 --> 00:15:42,600
You don't get it?

254
00:15:43,120 --> 00:15:43,960
Just the new boss making his mark.

255
00:15:44,159 --> 00:15:44,480
Hurry up.

256
00:16:07,639 --> 00:16:08,480
Can you keep it down?

257
00:16:09,159 --> 00:16:10,480
You totally ruined my train of thought.

258
00:16:11,799 --> 00:16:12,759
Let me tell you.

259
00:16:13,039 --> 00:16:13,799
I get it now.

260
00:16:14,279 --> 00:16:15,080
I completely get it.

261
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,440
It's not that I can't write it.

262
00:16:17,159 --> 00:16:18,200
I just don't want to.

263
00:16:18,399 --> 00:16:19,039
Then don't write it.

264
00:16:19,279 --> 00:16:19,759
Wrong.

265
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:21,200
Not only am I going to write it,

266
00:16:21,879 --> 00:16:23,399
I'm going to make it brilliant.

267
00:16:32,159 --> 00:16:33,960
My self-reflection report.

268
00:16:34,799 --> 00:16:36,360
I thought you'd had some huge revelation.

269
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:38,679
Found it.

270
00:16:39,559 --> 00:16:40,679
Here's another one. Want it?

271
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,320
No.

272
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:44,600
Sent it to your phone.

273
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,120
For when you finally 'get it,'

274
00:16:46,399 --> 00:16:46,879
it'll come in handy.

275
00:17:07,799 --> 00:17:08,599
Not bad, rookie.

276
00:17:09,559 --> 00:17:10,480
Scribbling away, huh?

277
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:11,880
Such talent.

278
00:17:13,759 --> 00:17:14,839
Way better than your boss.

279
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:39,759
Stop acting. Give it here, I'll do it.

280
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,119
Thanks.

281
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,200
Just four words?

282
00:17:48,039 --> 00:17:49,039
No wonder you're better than me.

283
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,039
I'm telling you,

284
00:17:51,319 --> 00:17:52,200
I'm definitely not slacking off.

285
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,559
It's mainly because this weekend,

286
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:54,960
I promised my wife

287
00:17:55,279 --> 00:17:57,240
to take the kids out to play.

288
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:02,440
Are you hungry? I'll go buy you some food.

289
00:18:02,599 --> 00:18:03,039
Not hungry.

290
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:05,039
I mean, what is Commissar Tan thinking?

291
00:18:05,559 --> 00:18:06,680
What's the use of writing this stuff?

292
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,880
Whether it's useful doesn't matter.

293
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,680
What you write doesn't matter either.

294
00:18:17,839 --> 00:18:18,559
The key is

295
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:20,599
whether you listen to him

296
00:18:21,119 --> 00:18:22,720
and submit the report on time.

297
00:18:29,119 --> 00:18:29,680
Got it.

298
00:18:31,119 --> 00:18:32,200
A compliance test.

299
00:18:33,079 --> 00:18:34,079
Then I'll just write whatever.

300
00:18:34,079 --> 00:18:34,720
You can write whatever,

301
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,680
but definitely don't half-ass my copy.

302
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:45,759
Will Captain Liao write it?

303
00:18:49,359 --> 00:18:49,759
Take a guess.

304
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:53,000
I really can't write this thing of yours.

305
00:18:53,119 --> 00:18:53,839
Don't know how?

306
00:18:54,039 --> 00:18:55,039
I'll help you.

307
00:18:55,039 --> 00:18:55,799
201.

308
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:59,839
Writing your ideological report is useless.

309
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,039
If you think

310
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:03,920
this training of mine

311
00:19:04,759 --> 00:19:05,559
is also useless,

312
00:19:06,319 --> 00:19:07,400
you don't have to participate.

313
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:09,799
I think this training method of yours

314
00:19:09,799 --> 00:19:10,559
is very useful.

315
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:12,400
Didn't I say it this afternoon?

316
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:14,599
Right now, in terms of fitness and...

317
00:19:14,599 --> 00:19:15,440
and skills,

318
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,960
we're doing very well.

319
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:18,759
It's just that this ideological work,

320
00:19:19,559 --> 00:19:20,880
we need to take it seriously.

321
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:23,799
You've done over 210 in this set.

322
00:19:24,599 --> 00:19:25,480
I really can't write it.

323
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:29,359
Your muscles...

324
00:19:29,519 --> 00:19:31,119
they're really popping. Popping.

325
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:32,720
These triceps.

326
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:33,599
These... these biceps.

327
00:19:33,799 --> 00:19:35,440
This definition is so beautiful.

328
00:19:36,319 --> 00:19:37,039
You should take the lead.

329
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,400
The whole team is watching you.

330
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:40,720
Please cooperate with my work.

331
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,960
How much willpower would it take...

332
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:47,279
Could I... could I build, in half a year,

333
00:19:47,279 --> 00:19:48,079
definition like yours?

334
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:50,240
No.

335
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:51,279
Falsification.

336
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:54,000
It's a reference.

337
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,640
The whole team is watching me too.

338
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:58,440
You have high awareness.

339
00:19:58,440 --> 00:19:59,400
Your ideology has no issues.

340
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,200
But that doesn't mean others don't.

341
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,599
Otherwise, why would the leaders...

342
00:20:02,799 --> 00:20:04,920
have me focus on ideological work?

343
00:20:05,599 --> 00:20:06,079
Alright.

344
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:08,799
It's just the two of us in this room.

345
00:20:09,559 --> 00:20:10,759
We're both in the SWAT team.

346
00:20:11,680 --> 00:20:13,279
If you really want everyone to respect you,

347
00:20:14,599 --> 00:20:16,279
then stop doing superficial work.

348
00:20:16,279 --> 00:20:17,279
Do something practical.

349
00:20:19,440 --> 00:20:21,079
Tell me, what's practical?

350
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:28,240
Our SWAT team...

351
00:20:28,559 --> 00:20:30,400
lacks facilities and equipment.

352
00:20:31,759 --> 00:20:33,839
We even borrow the firehouse to rappel.

353
00:20:34,279 --> 00:20:35,160
What? Rap...

354
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,319
Rappel training.

355
00:20:37,279 --> 00:20:37,839
Rappelling.

356
00:20:40,599 --> 00:20:42,640
So these things are very important now.

357
00:20:46,279 --> 00:20:47,000
Very important.

358
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,400
I've noted it all down.

359
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:53,000
Captain Liao,

360
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:55,359
I must emphasize...

361
00:20:55,559 --> 00:20:57,319
No, I have to correct you on this.

362
00:20:58,079 --> 00:20:59,880
Ideological work is not

363
00:21:01,319 --> 00:21:02,480
optional.

364
00:21:04,319 --> 00:21:05,519
It's a top priority.

365
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,759
You can look down on me,

366
00:21:11,559 --> 00:21:12,960
but you can't look down on my work.

367
00:21:14,759 --> 00:21:15,559
This is very serious.

368
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,039
Commissar Tan,

369
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:26,440
you don't

370
00:21:27,279 --> 00:21:28,759
seem like you're here to pad your resume.

371
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:32,079
Don't ask for trouble here for nothing.

372
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,880
Why are you asking for trouble here?

373
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:33,480
I sent you to the SWAT team to fix them.

374
00:23:34,559 --> 00:23:36,240
Don't turn into a virus yourself.

375
00:23:38,599 --> 00:23:40,759
If you still rely on old superficial tricks

376
00:23:41,319 --> 00:23:42,640
to just go through the motions here,

377
00:23:43,519 --> 00:23:44,279
I can't guarantee

378
00:23:45,359 --> 00:23:46,680
you'll be able to come back in two years.

379
00:24:12,400 --> 00:24:12,960
Commissar Tan.

380
00:24:14,359 --> 00:24:15,240
What are you doing?

381
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:16,240
I can tidy up myself.

382
00:24:18,359 --> 00:24:19,440
I'm not tidying up for you.

383
00:24:20,759 --> 00:24:22,119
We're roommates from now on.

384
00:24:24,079 --> 00:24:25,519
I'm moving in tonight.

385
00:24:27,559 --> 00:24:28,680
Do you normally snore?

386
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:30,240
I don't know.

387
00:24:32,079 --> 00:24:33,160
I'll move out right now.

388
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,599
Don't want to live with your Commissar?

389
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:35,960
No desire to advance?

390
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:39,559
Relax.

391
00:24:41,119 --> 00:24:41,960
At work,

392
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:44,640
we are superior and subordinate.

393
00:24:45,559 --> 00:24:46,640
But back in the dorm,

394
00:24:47,079 --> 00:24:48,000
we're just roommates.

395
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:50,119
If you want to advance,

396
00:24:51,319 --> 00:24:52,319
stick close to me.

397
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:55,400
Then I'll take the top bunk.

398
00:24:56,599 --> 00:24:58,720
There's no rank in the dorm!

399
00:25:00,519 --> 00:25:01,480
I just like sleeping on the top bunk.

400
00:25:02,119 --> 00:25:02,480
Really.

401
00:25:06,920 --> 00:25:08,359
He moved into Wang Yunsheng's room.

402
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:13,279
He just had me move a desk for him.

403
00:25:17,880 --> 00:25:18,680
Are you two alright?

404
00:25:20,279 --> 00:25:20,839
We're fine.

405
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:23,759
Did he say anything to you?

406
00:25:23,960 --> 00:25:24,640
Just a few words.

407
00:25:25,119 --> 00:25:28,240
Said he wants to take root at the base.

408
00:25:29,079 --> 00:25:33,160
And eat and live with the regular guys.

409
00:25:33,759 --> 00:25:35,440
To experience what they feel firsthand.

410
00:25:43,160 --> 00:25:44,160
Putting on a show again.

411
00:25:44,799 --> 00:25:45,960
Why overthink it?

412
00:25:47,160 --> 00:25:48,160
Who cares if it's a show?

413
00:25:49,039 --> 00:25:49,759
Just remember,

414
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:51,799
as long as he doesn't delay our training,

415
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:53,400
we're good.

416
00:25:55,680 --> 00:25:56,799
Two years

417
00:25:58,240 --> 00:25:59,319
will pass in a flash.

418
00:26:02,440 --> 00:26:03,039
What are you doing?

419
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:04,160
Picking up a package.

420
00:26:10,240 --> 00:26:10,880
Wait a minute.

421
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:12,599
Captain Liao.

422
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:13,680
Up so late?

423
00:26:14,960 --> 00:26:16,160
Bought a toy for Naonao.

424
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:18,440
Where's Naonao?

425
00:26:18,720 --> 00:26:19,079
Asleep.

426
00:26:19,240 --> 00:26:20,000
He's already asleep.

427
00:26:21,279 --> 00:26:22,440
Doesn't he like airplanes?

428
00:26:22,559 --> 00:26:23,480
I bought one for him.

429
00:26:24,079 --> 00:26:25,640
Thanks, Captain Liao. Very thoughtful.

430
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:26,200
Don't mention it.

431
00:26:30,359 --> 00:26:31,640
Tom Hardy?

432
00:26:34,480 --> 00:26:35,319
It's my screen name.

433
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:39,079
Tom Hardy, I know him.

434
00:26:39,319 --> 00:26:42,799
That British actor, right?

435
00:26:42,799 --> 00:26:44,000
He has a very unique look.

436
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:44,440
Right.

437
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:45,400
Venom.

438
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:46,680
Yes, yes, that's him!

439
00:26:47,799 --> 00:26:49,079
Why pick that name?

440
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,799
They all say we look quite alike.

441
00:26:57,599 --> 00:26:58,799
You do look a bit alike.

442
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:00,160
Right?

443
00:27:01,079 --> 00:27:03,640
Alright then, I'll go back and rest.

444
00:27:05,039 --> 00:27:06,400
Thanks, Tom Hardy.

445
00:27:10,359 --> 00:27:11,559
Tom Hardy.

446
00:27:18,160 --> 00:27:20,279
How's the progress on Dai Mingming's case?

447
00:27:21,319 --> 00:27:22,480
It's been transferred to CID.

448
00:27:23,799 --> 00:27:24,960
Mingming's mom is in the detention center.

449
00:27:25,799 --> 00:27:27,039
Mingming's at the welfare home for now.

450
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:28,640
Now we're just waiting for the trial.

451
00:27:30,039 --> 00:27:32,279
Chief Ji has been in a bad mood lately.

452
00:27:34,799 --> 00:27:37,599
Chief Ji isn't handling this anymore.

453
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,279
I heard from Li Zhi

454
00:27:41,240 --> 00:27:42,839
that Chief Ji will visit the city bureau

455
00:27:43,079 --> 00:27:44,079
next week to report on Dai Mingming's case.

456
00:27:50,119 --> 00:27:50,960
What day is he going?

457
00:27:53,079 --> 00:27:53,480
Monday.

458
00:27:53,799 --> 00:27:54,680
He should go right after his shift starts.

459
00:27:58,319 --> 00:27:59,799
This case wasn't supposed to get this far.

460
00:28:01,759 --> 00:28:03,039
It's my fault I brought Mingming here.

461
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:10,400
Commissar Tan,

462
00:28:13,119 --> 00:28:14,799
have I completely disappointed Chief Ji?

463
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,319
Yunsheng, do you want to change

464
00:28:29,319 --> 00:28:31,000
how Chief Ji sees you?

465
00:28:34,720 --> 00:28:35,079
I do.

466
00:28:40,039 --> 00:28:40,759
I know a way.

467
00:29:02,799 --> 00:29:03,359
Come in.

468
00:29:03,839 --> 00:29:04,319
Commissar Tan.

469
00:29:05,279 --> 00:29:06,480
Xiao Lu, need something?

470
00:29:06,680 --> 00:29:07,480
I need to ask for leave.

471
00:29:07,839 --> 00:29:08,680
My mom is sick.

472
00:29:10,079 --> 00:29:10,799
Which hospital?

473
00:29:11,039 --> 00:29:11,559
She's in Lvteng.

474
00:29:12,119 --> 00:29:12,799
Is it serious?

475
00:29:13,359 --> 00:29:14,000
It's not serious.

476
00:29:14,519 --> 00:29:15,640
It's just I'm from a single-parent family,

477
00:29:15,839 --> 00:29:16,799
and I'm an only child.

478
00:29:18,119 --> 00:29:19,559
Right, that's a tricky situation.

479
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:22,519
I'll have the admin staff buy some things

480
00:29:22,519 --> 00:29:24,240
and visit your mom on behalf of the unit.

481
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:25,559
No need for the trouble.

482
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:26,680
I'll be quick.

483
00:29:27,200 --> 00:29:28,359
I finished my report. Please take a look.

484
00:29:38,119 --> 00:29:38,759
Alright.

485
00:29:39,079 --> 00:29:40,160
The writing is fluent.

486
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:41,839
The logic is clear.

487
00:29:42,039 --> 00:29:42,440
Good.

488
00:29:43,599 --> 00:29:44,119
Good.

489
00:29:46,119 --> 00:29:47,160
What a perfect template.

490
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:50,559
Then... did I pass, Commissar Tan?

491
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:55,359
Xiao Lu.

492
00:29:56,720 --> 00:29:57,920
I'm sure that

493
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:59,599
a top Police University student like you

494
00:29:59,799 --> 00:30:00,880
can definitely write one

495
00:30:00,920 --> 00:30:02,480
that's even better than this template.

496
00:30:06,720 --> 00:30:08,039
Commissar Tan, what about my leave?

497
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:11,480
I'll approve it after you rewrite it.

498
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:15,279
Thank you, Commissar Tan.

499
00:30:17,279 --> 00:30:18,240
I'm heading to the city bureau

500
00:30:18,839 --> 00:30:19,599
for a meeting.

501
00:30:23,279 --> 00:30:25,559
Hurry up. Don't delay visiting your mom.

502
00:30:40,079 --> 00:30:40,920
Where did the boss go?

503
00:30:41,920 --> 00:30:42,759
To a meeting at the city bureau.

504
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:50,640
He didn't approve your leave, did he?

505
00:30:52,119 --> 00:30:52,680
He did.

506
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:53,559
He did?

507
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:55,240
Once I finish writing.

508
00:30:58,160 --> 00:30:58,920
Writing what?

509
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:00,160
I got busted.

510
00:31:04,759 --> 00:31:05,839
Then mine is probably doomed too.

511
00:31:06,920 --> 00:31:07,680
Yours is fine.

512
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:09,559
I copied the one from 2018.

513
00:31:09,759 --> 00:31:10,680
Yours is from 2017.

514
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:11,440
He won't remember.

515
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:14,119
What nonsense is that? Come back here!

516
00:31:17,119 --> 00:31:18,279
Rewrite it. Hurry up.

517
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:21,039
So annoying.

518
00:31:26,359 --> 00:31:26,920
Commissar Tan.

519
00:31:31,079 --> 00:31:32,680
Commissar Tan, long time no see.

520
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:34,039
Long time no see.

521
00:31:41,039 --> 00:31:41,480
Ji Min.

522
00:31:41,720 --> 00:31:43,640
You're going to see Chief Guo, aren't you?

523
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:45,480
I heard from Wang Yunsheng.

524
00:31:45,559 --> 00:31:46,359
I'll go with you.

525
00:31:47,559 --> 00:31:49,839
Tan Yan, I appreciate your kindness.

526
00:31:50,119 --> 00:31:51,039
You can't help with this.

527
00:31:54,200 --> 00:31:54,680
Ji Min.

528
00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:55,759
Ji Min.

529
00:31:56,759 --> 00:31:58,039
Let me show you a video.

530
00:32:02,839 --> 00:32:05,119
Over the weekend, Wang Yunsheng and I

531
00:32:05,200 --> 00:32:06,839
tracked down Dai Yumei's neighbors.

532
00:32:07,119 --> 00:32:09,240
Mom left me with Aunt Dai when she worked.

533
00:32:10,079 --> 00:32:11,519
Aunt Dai always used to say,

534
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:13,200
taking care of one is the same

535
00:32:13,319 --> 00:32:14,200
as taking care of two.

536
00:32:14,519 --> 00:32:15,039
Don't worry.

537
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:17,559
I sincerely hope the government

538
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:22,039
considers Dai Yumei turning herself in

539
00:32:23,720 --> 00:32:24,920
and be lenient with her.

540
00:32:30,920 --> 00:32:32,200
You two, one from the local station,

541
00:32:33,119 --> 00:32:34,079
one from the SWAT team.

542
00:32:34,559 --> 00:32:36,400
What kind of duo is this?

543
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:38,960
It's just a coincidence.

544
00:32:39,359 --> 00:32:40,200
A coincidence?

545
00:32:43,680 --> 00:32:45,759
Before transferring to the local station,

546
00:32:45,759 --> 00:32:47,160
he was in our SWAT detachment.

547
00:32:47,799 --> 00:32:49,000
This is also his first case.

548
00:32:49,640 --> 00:32:50,680
As his political commissar,

549
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:52,200
it's my duty to look out for him.

550
00:32:52,839 --> 00:32:53,319
Chief Guo.

551
00:32:54,200 --> 00:32:55,599
Sentencing Dai Yumei is easy.

552
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,640
But she has late-stage cancer.

553
00:32:57,960 --> 00:33:00,200
Punishing her holds no real significance.

554
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:02,960
Plus, Dai Mingming is a special needs kid.

555
00:33:03,720 --> 00:33:05,640
If it weren't for Dai Yumei,

556
00:33:06,400 --> 00:33:07,839
he couldn't take care of himself at all.

557
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,640
There's a great saying.

558
00:33:12,079 --> 00:33:13,200
It says the law

559
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:14,799
doesn't just have

560
00:33:15,119 --> 00:33:16,119
a cold side.

561
00:33:17,319 --> 00:33:18,559
It has a warm side too.

562
00:33:19,759 --> 00:33:20,599
Well said, right?

563
00:33:22,839 --> 00:33:23,319
Very well.

564
00:33:27,319 --> 00:33:28,440
How is this a coincidence?

565
00:33:28,960 --> 00:33:30,960
You planned this, singing the same tune.

566
00:33:32,079 --> 00:33:33,000
We really didn't plan this.

567
00:33:33,839 --> 00:33:35,680
Alright, I understand the case now.

568
00:33:37,039 --> 00:33:38,599
I have to say, it is quite special.

569
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:42,279
I'll send the video to you.

570
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:44,160
What?

571
00:33:45,359 --> 00:33:47,640
Do you two have any other coincidences?

572
00:33:48,519 --> 00:33:49,839
No. I have a meeting next.

573
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:50,960
No.

574
00:33:51,920 --> 00:33:52,839
Goodbye, Chief.

575
00:33:54,359 --> 00:33:55,160
Chief, look at me.

576
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:56,359
Haven't I lost a lot of weight?

577
00:33:58,279 --> 00:33:59,079
I can't tell.

578
00:33:59,079 --> 00:33:59,799
My belt is even looser.

579
00:34:00,039 --> 00:34:00,839
I've been working out.

580
00:34:01,240 --> 00:34:02,000
You need to keep at it.

581
00:34:02,839 --> 00:34:03,160
Let's go.

582
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:06,240
Alright, Chief Guo, we're heading out.

583
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:07,440
Thank you, Chief Guo.

584
00:34:11,440 --> 00:34:12,280
This couple...

585
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:15,599
What are they playing at?

586
00:34:16,199 --> 00:34:17,880
I didn't act on my own this time, did I?

587
00:34:18,480 --> 00:34:19,440
Barely.

588
00:34:20,280 --> 00:34:21,519
But this time, I really want to thank you.

589
00:34:22,199 --> 00:34:23,239
Don't mention it.

590
00:34:25,679 --> 00:34:27,840
I'm thanking you for Mingming and his mom.

591
00:34:28,960 --> 00:34:30,400
Time to eat. Let's get some food together.

592
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:42,039
I've got time.

593
00:34:44,679 --> 00:34:46,639
Last time they all thought we had a fight.

594
00:34:47,519 --> 00:34:48,039
Are you going?

595
00:34:49,960 --> 00:34:50,840
Why wouldn't I?

596
00:34:54,519 --> 00:34:54,920
Just wait.

597
00:34:55,119 --> 00:34:56,119
They aren't here yet.

598
00:34:56,480 --> 00:34:57,440
So unreliable.

599
00:34:59,000 --> 00:34:59,920
Who's unreliable?

600
00:34:59,920 --> 00:35:00,800
We're here, we're here.

601
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:01,280
Director Tan.

602
00:35:01,639 --> 00:35:02,079
Chief Ji.

603
00:35:02,239 --> 00:35:02,920
Take a seat, take a seat.

604
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:03,840
What's going on?

605
00:35:04,280 --> 00:35:05,239
You two came together?

606
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:07,119
Acting just like a married couple.

607
00:35:10,519 --> 00:35:12,679
We are a married couple, isn't it normal?

608
00:35:13,480 --> 00:35:14,199
It's normal.

609
00:35:14,519 --> 00:35:15,719
It's just that...

610
00:35:15,719 --> 00:35:16,679
...before this,

611
00:35:16,880 --> 00:35:17,440
...right?

612
00:35:17,960 --> 00:35:19,000
Either one arrives just before...

613
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:20,119
...or just after the other.

614
00:35:20,559 --> 00:35:21,400
Now that you're acting normal...

615
00:35:21,519 --> 00:35:22,360
...it actually seems abnormal.

616
00:35:23,199 --> 00:35:24,039
Are those two coming?

617
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:25,639
They're unreliable, I told you.

618
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:26,480
Are they coming or not?

619
00:35:26,519 --> 00:35:27,199
You better hurry up.

620
00:35:27,320 --> 00:35:28,000
Let's eat while we wait.

621
00:35:29,920 --> 00:35:30,559
Let's eat then.

622
00:35:30,639 --> 00:35:31,760
Eat, eat, eat.

623
00:35:32,440 --> 00:35:33,079
We'll eat while we wait.

624
00:35:34,519 --> 00:35:35,159
Don't burn your hands.

625
00:35:39,280 --> 00:35:40,320
I read this issue of the police magazine.

626
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:42,360
That big photo of you looks good.

627
00:35:42,840 --> 00:35:43,960
You look like a celebrity.

628
00:35:45,679 --> 00:35:46,599
Don't, don't bring it up.

629
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:48,480
The leadership chewed me out.

630
00:35:48,880 --> 00:35:50,199
They said I infected...

631
00:35:51,559 --> 00:35:52,480
...the entire SWAT detachment.

632
00:35:55,599 --> 00:35:56,800
Hurry and help me think of a way.

633
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:58,559
How to assert authority on the SWAT team.

634
00:35:59,159 --> 00:36:00,000
What way can I think of for you?

635
00:36:00,679 --> 00:36:02,199
Isn't asserting authority your forte?

636
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:05,519
The key isn't asserting authority.

637
00:36:06,039 --> 00:36:06,639
It's winning them over.

638
00:36:07,159 --> 00:36:07,719
Those are two different things.

639
00:36:09,840 --> 00:36:10,559
Look at him.

640
00:36:10,679 --> 00:36:11,800
Just look at what Old Ji said.

641
00:36:12,360 --> 00:36:13,760
He always hits the nail on the head.

642
00:36:14,679 --> 00:36:15,400
No, what's going on with you?

643
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:17,039
Your previous trick...

644
00:36:17,159 --> 00:36:18,519
...of playing the big boss didn't work?

645
00:36:21,320 --> 00:36:22,199
It's not working anymore.

646
00:36:22,760 --> 00:36:23,920
The leaders called me a...

647
00:36:24,159 --> 00:36:24,800
...virus.

648
00:36:25,239 --> 00:36:26,199
Do you think it's working?

649
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:27,760
You really are a virus.

650
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:29,239
So tonight...

651
00:36:29,599 --> 00:36:31,079
I need you guys to help me brainstorm.

652
00:36:31,480 --> 00:36:32,000
Think of a way.

653
00:36:33,519 --> 00:36:34,880
Are they coming? Call and hurry them up.

654
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:36,039
We're all here.

655
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:37,800
Coming, coming, we're here.

656
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:39,239
You better hurry up.

657
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:40,199
So unreliable.

658
00:36:40,199 --> 00:36:41,320
Way too unreliable.

659
00:36:41,320 --> 00:36:41,840
What happened?

660
00:36:41,840 --> 00:36:42,559
We went to line up.

661
00:36:42,719 --> 00:36:43,599
Lined up to buy some braised meat.

662
00:36:43,679 --> 00:36:44,480
Come on, try some.

663
00:36:44,480 --> 00:36:45,280
Here, here, take this.

664
00:36:45,280 --> 00:36:46,840
You two look pretty put together today.

665
00:36:47,599 --> 00:36:49,320
What do you mean put together? Clothes?

666
00:36:49,719 --> 00:36:51,840
No, you two really are put together today.

667
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:52,280
Right?

668
00:36:52,559 --> 00:36:53,639
They're a married couple.

669
00:36:53,960 --> 00:36:55,199
What's wrong with being put together?

670
00:36:55,239 --> 00:36:55,960
Just stop talking.

671
00:36:55,960 --> 00:36:56,880
I hate hearing you talk.

672
00:36:57,119 --> 00:36:57,599
It's so annoying.

673
00:36:57,639 --> 00:36:58,480
What's the occasion today?

674
00:36:59,119 --> 00:37:00,800
Is there some good news to celebrate?

675
00:37:00,880 --> 00:37:01,480
Such a feast.

676
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:02,480
Didn't you read the police magazine?

677
00:37:02,840 --> 00:37:03,559
Old Tan is front and center.

678
00:37:04,360 --> 00:37:04,800
Really?

679
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:05,119
Of course.

680
00:37:05,559 --> 00:37:06,000
You saw it?

681
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:06,480
I saw it.

682
00:37:06,920 --> 00:37:07,320
Did you?

683
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:09,519
Don't mention this front and center thing.

684
00:37:09,639 --> 00:37:10,280
Let me tell you,

685
00:37:10,880 --> 00:37:11,760
Old Tan is finished.

686
00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:13,440
What happened to you?

687
00:37:15,599 --> 00:37:17,320
He can't establish his authority.

688
00:37:21,480 --> 00:37:24,199
He wants to assert authority on the team,

689
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:24,880
but he can't.

690
00:37:24,880 --> 00:37:26,119
He wants us to think of something.

691
00:37:26,800 --> 00:37:27,559
S-SWAT team...

692
00:37:27,840 --> 00:37:28,960
Isn't that simple?

693
00:37:29,480 --> 00:37:31,039
You... when you go to the SWAT team,

694
00:37:31,039 --> 00:37:33,199
you can't lower yourself to their level.

695
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:35,039
You have to hold your head high.

696
00:37:35,039 --> 00:37:36,079
You need to make them look up to you.

697
00:37:36,079 --> 00:37:37,119
But honestly,

698
00:37:37,480 --> 00:37:38,760
those SWAT boys,

699
00:37:39,079 --> 00:37:39,400
sometimes,

700
00:37:39,400 --> 00:37:40,719
you need a little whip behind them.

701
00:37:41,239 --> 00:37:41,960
You have to whip them.

702
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:43,599
I did. I whipped them plenty.

703
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:44,840
It doesn't work.

704
00:37:45,079 --> 00:37:47,400
We gotta serve them something tough.

705
00:37:47,920 --> 00:37:48,559
Think of a way.

706
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:51,000
What way can we think of?

707
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:52,840
We... we can go show our support for you.

708
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:54,159
Forget it, what support?

709
00:37:54,400 --> 00:37:54,800
What?

710
00:37:55,039 --> 00:37:56,440
With Liao Bufan's terrible temper,

711
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:57,400
would he show any of us respect?

712
00:37:57,639 --> 00:37:58,159
Would he respect you?

713
00:37:58,159 --> 00:37:59,880
Hey, hey, don't say 'us'.

714
00:38:00,039 --> 00:38:00,920
It has nothing to do with us.

715
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:02,400
What's the main reason here?

716
00:38:02,519 --> 00:38:03,800
You get no respect.

717
00:38:05,519 --> 00:38:06,079
Get outta here.

718
00:38:06,079 --> 00:38:07,400
I really hate hearing you talk.

719
00:38:08,039 --> 00:38:09,320
Do I need his respect?

720
00:38:09,920 --> 00:38:11,119
He's just so simple-minded every day...

721
00:38:11,119 --> 00:38:12,159
and completely unreasonable.

722
00:38:12,559 --> 00:38:13,119
Right?

723
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:13,679
Exactly.

724
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:15,719
Right now, that Liao kid

725
00:38:16,679 --> 00:38:18,320
has made a mess of the SWAT detachment.

726
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,119
His personal style is too strong.

727
00:38:20,639 --> 00:38:21,679
Tough to handle, very tough.

728
00:38:22,119 --> 00:38:23,159
Let me remind you, Old Tan.

729
00:38:24,039 --> 00:38:25,400
You bring this anxiety upon yourself.

730
00:38:26,159 --> 00:38:27,239
Yesterday it was Zhao Guohua.

731
00:38:28,079 --> 00:38:29,079
Today it's Liao Bufan.

732
00:38:29,599 --> 00:38:30,320
And tomorrow?

733
00:38:41,320 --> 00:38:42,079
Zhao Guohua.

734
00:38:43,079 --> 00:38:44,039
Just pick it up.

735
00:38:49,119 --> 00:38:49,599
Chief Zhao.

736
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:50,599
I heard them say

737
00:38:50,599 --> 00:38:52,519
you're at the Little Courtyard Farmhouse?

738
00:38:52,639 --> 00:38:53,639
I'm... I'm here too.

739
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:54,920
You're at the Little Courtyard too?

740
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:56,280
Wait, where are you?

741
00:38:56,440 --> 00:38:57,280
Which room?

742
00:38:59,880 --> 00:39:00,679
I'm right here.

743
00:39:04,239 --> 00:39:05,000
Chief Zhao, Chief Zhao.

744
00:39:07,280 --> 00:39:07,719
Captain Zhang.

745
00:39:08,039 --> 00:39:08,440
Captain Na.

746
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:09,920
Commissar Tan.

747
00:39:10,719 --> 00:39:11,039
Sister-in-law.

748
00:39:12,360 --> 00:39:13,480
You guys are really here.

749
00:39:13,960 --> 00:39:14,480
That's great.

750
00:39:14,719 --> 00:39:16,239
Smooth sailing, smooth sailing.

751
00:39:16,960 --> 00:39:17,400
Well,

752
00:39:18,800 --> 00:39:19,320
have a seat.

753
00:39:21,360 --> 00:39:22,800
I... I won't. I've been sitting all day.

754
00:39:29,239 --> 00:39:31,360
Today... It's such a coincidence today.

755
00:39:31,519 --> 00:39:33,400
I'm right next door. Right next door.

756
00:39:33,880 --> 00:39:35,119
And their boss told me

757
00:39:35,119 --> 00:39:35,960
that you were here.

758
00:39:36,199 --> 00:39:36,920
I said, 'Really?'

759
00:39:37,760 --> 00:39:38,920
Because who have I been trying to invite?

760
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:40,119
I've been trying to invite Captain Na.

761
00:39:40,360 --> 00:39:40,880
Right.

762
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:42,239
I've kept in touch with Captain Na.

763
00:39:42,400 --> 00:39:43,320
But you know how it is at work.

764
00:39:44,519 --> 00:39:45,360
Work is just too busy.

765
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:47,440
Yeah.

766
00:39:47,679 --> 00:39:49,239
Running into you here, what a coincidence.

767
00:39:55,280 --> 00:39:55,760
Commissar Tan,

768
00:39:55,760 --> 00:39:56,320
have you

769
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:57,880
moved into the SWAT base now?

770
00:40:06,119 --> 00:40:07,760
I have moved into the SWAT base.

771
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:10,559
Putting duty before family.

772
00:40:10,920 --> 00:40:12,320
Eating, sleeping, and training together.

773
00:40:13,519 --> 00:40:14,480
It's a special period.

774
00:40:15,199 --> 00:40:17,000
My family understands and supports it.

775
00:40:18,719 --> 00:40:19,679
Since I just arrived at the SWAT base,

776
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:21,559
if I want to win them over, I have to

777
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:22,679
lead by example.

778
00:40:24,719 --> 00:40:25,760
Indeed, indeed.

779
00:40:25,960 --> 00:40:27,039
Because last time, so coincidentally,

780
00:40:27,039 --> 00:40:28,440
I went to the SWAT base and saw him

781
00:40:28,519 --> 00:40:29,519
running behind the team.

782
00:40:30,920 --> 00:40:31,559
Indeed.

783
00:40:32,079 --> 00:40:33,079
Grab some chopsticks and have a bite.

784
00:40:36,119 --> 00:40:36,880
How about this, how about this.

785
00:40:37,599 --> 00:40:38,199
I'll use this

786
00:40:38,800 --> 00:40:39,320
tea.

787
00:40:39,519 --> 00:40:40,480
Let me pour it, let me pour it.

788
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:43,199
Thank you, Commissar Tan.

789
00:40:44,639 --> 00:40:45,440
I'll substitute tea for liquor.

790
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:47,440
So,

791
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:48,280
I'll

792
00:40:49,079 --> 00:40:50,079
raise a glass to everyone.

793
00:41:06,360 --> 00:41:07,199
Unload everything.

794
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:08,480
Careful not to damage anything.

795
00:41:12,079 --> 00:41:12,480
Ma'am.

796
00:41:13,679 --> 00:41:14,480
Naonao, go play in your room.

797
00:41:18,159 --> 00:41:18,960
What's the meaning of this?

798
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:22,360
These are the things you use at home.

799
00:41:22,840 --> 00:41:24,719
Mr. Lu told me to bring them over to you.

800
00:41:24,880 --> 00:41:26,159
No need. Take them back.

801
00:41:27,320 --> 00:41:28,400
Please don't make this hard for me.

802
00:41:29,039 --> 00:41:30,079
You know Mr. Lu's temper.

803
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:31,679
If you don't accept them,

804
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:33,119
he'll make me deliver them every day.

805
00:41:39,039 --> 00:41:40,559
This is a gift from Mr. Lu.

806
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:42,000
It's this year's latest model.

807
00:41:42,880 --> 00:41:43,480
He said

808
00:41:44,079 --> 00:41:45,800
he hasn't forgotten what he promised you.

809
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:54,559
By the way, Ma'am.

810
00:41:54,960 --> 00:41:56,320
We rented a place right across the street.

811
00:41:56,960 --> 00:41:59,199
We figured if anything happens at the shop,

812
00:41:59,320 --> 00:42:00,000
we'd be close by to help out.

813
00:42:01,039 --> 00:42:01,840
Mr. Lu also left instructions.

814
00:42:02,559 --> 00:42:03,400
Whatever you'd like to eat from now on,

815
00:42:03,840 --> 00:42:04,639
three meals a day,

816
00:42:04,920 --> 00:42:05,880
we'll make it and deliver it to you.

817
00:42:06,400 --> 00:42:07,159
Not necessary.

818
00:42:12,480 --> 00:42:13,639
The SWAT team is right across the street.

819
00:42:14,840 --> 00:42:15,480
I'm warning you,

820
00:42:16,239 --> 00:42:16,880
don't try anything.

821
00:42:21,239 --> 00:42:22,760
We just rented a place across the street.

822
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:25,119
Like the SWAT team can do anything.

823
00:42:30,159 --> 00:42:30,760
Alright, Ma'am.

824
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:31,559
I'll leave you to it.

825
00:42:32,559 --> 00:42:33,719
Call me anytime if you need anything.

826
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:49,719
Mom.

827
00:43:12,079 --> 00:43:12,840
Where's Lu Xiao?

828
00:43:13,239 --> 00:43:13,800
He's on leave.

829
00:43:14,400 --> 00:43:15,159
His mom is sick.

830
00:43:15,320 --> 00:43:16,639
Tonight's mission: patrol and inspect.

831
00:43:16,800 --> 00:43:18,000
Mingliu Club.

832
00:43:18,199 --> 00:43:19,400
Heavy foot traffic.

833
00:43:19,880 --> 00:43:21,920
It's our key focus.

834
00:43:21,920 --> 00:43:23,119
But I can't guarantee

835
00:43:23,199 --> 00:43:25,360
that all incoming guests are clean.

836
00:43:26,199 --> 00:43:27,719
A 2,000-word self-criticism.

837
00:43:27,719 --> 00:43:29,480
A bureau-wide reprimand.

838
00:43:29,679 --> 00:43:30,199
Hurry up and apologize.

839
00:43:30,519 --> 00:43:31,679
What did I do wrong?

840
00:43:31,719 --> 00:43:33,320
Captain Liao, something's up with Naonao.

841
00:43:33,760 --> 00:43:35,360
Can you hear Mommy?

842
00:43:35,360 --> 00:43:36,079
Can you hear me?
